hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"293","We are Abdullah bin Hashim, we are Bahz, meaning the blind son of Asad, we are Ikrimah bin Ammar, we are Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, On the authority of his uncle Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting in the mosque and his companions were with him, when a Bedouin came. Then he urinated in the mosque, and his companions said: “No, no.” Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to his companions: “Do not force him, leave him.” Then he called him and said: “Indeed, This mosque is not suitable for any filth or urine, or as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, it is only for reading the Qur’an. And the remembrance of God and prayer.” Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to a man from among the people: “Get up and bring us a bucket of water and pour it over him.” So he came. With a bucket of water, he poured it on him"
